  "script": "543 horsepower, but more interesting than that is the weight. That's the secret of the 2024 BMW M3 CS. Made only during 2024, it's limited, reducing weight using carbon fiber. The 3.0L twin-turbo I6 engine churns out 543 hp and 479 lb-ft of torque. It's not just about speed, but control. Carbon ceramic brakes and a carbon fiber roof. Vital for weight reduction and handling precision. Inside, advanced tech includes a Harman Kardon system and M carbon bucket seats. Comfort meets performance. The AWD system ensures power meets pavement effectively. It\u2019s all about traction and control. Does the M3 CS offer too much for the street, or is it the ultimate track-ready sedan? What do you think?",
